{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01X1HXfKHJbiTZjqEL3ej3L5","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# OntoCoDec — Paper Framing\n2\t\n3\t## Target Venue\n4\tEMNLP 2026 (ARR submission May 25, 2026) — **目标: conference main**（D040, 用户明确指示）\n5\t\n6\t## Title\n7\tOntoCoDec: Type-Valid Information Extraction via Compiled Ontology Constraints\n8\t(D015: \"Near-Complete\" dropped — DocRED residual DR=10.21% (Qwen) 不算 near-complete。论文贡献是方法，不是特定消除率。SciERC 0.93% 和 DocRED 2.55% (Llama) 可在正文中描述为 near-complete，但 title 不宜 overclaim。)\n9\t\n10\t**D040 Story 升级方向**: 从 \"IE-specific constrained decoding\" → \"universal ontology-constrained structured generation framework\"。WikiEvents Event Extraction 验证跨任务泛化。Continuation masking v2 突破（10-doc: RoV 0%, semantic violations ↓95.8%）初步确认跨任务有效性，全量实验进行中。最终 title 待全量结果后调整。\n11\t\n12\t## Core Insight\n13\tLLM-based IE systems produce systematic ontology constraint violations concentrated in specific relation types. Prompt-level intervention (schema-informed prompting) reduces violations by ~62% but cannot eliminate them — certain relation types retain 25-30% violation rates even with explicit constraint descriptions. OntoCoDec provides **near-complete elimination (DR 15.4%→0.93%, ↓94%) at zero or positive F1 impact** through automatic ontology-to-decoder constraint compilation with two complementary layers.\n14\t\n15\t**Phase 2 confirmed (D012 bootstrap CI, v2 fix)**: Grammar+Semantic dual-layer constrained decoding reduces domain/range violations by 94%, eliminates entity-type and relation-vocabulary violations entirely (→0%). F1 impact is **dataset-dependent**:\n16\t- SciERC: Rel F1 neutral (+0.13pp, p=0.58), Ent F1 neutral (-0.03pp, p=0.53)\n17\t- DocRED: Rel F1 **significantly improved** (+0.50pp, p<0.001, 95% CI [+0.23, +0.81]); Ent F1 **significantly improved** (+1.23pp, p<0.001, 95% CI [+0.94, +1.55])\n18\t- Mechanism: grammar 消除 OOV relation names (DocRED RV 29.66%→0.03%) + 非标 entity types (ET 2.48%→0%)。all_set F1 方法下 OOV=FP → fewer FP → higher precision/F1。SciERC baseline RV/ET 已很低，效果不显著。\n19\t- **Grammar 层是 F1 提升的唯一来源**: grammar_only Ent F1=59.38% ≈ full_s1 59.37% (Δ+0.01pp, p=0.66)。Semantic 层对 F1 无额外贡献，专注 DR reduction。\n20\t\n21\t## Core Claims\n22\t\n23\t### Claim 1 (Empirical): Violation Landscape\n24\tLLM-based IE systems violate ontology type constraints at non-trivial rates (15.4% per-triple on SciERC, 18.7% on DocRED). Violations are **not uniformly distributed** — they concentrate on relation types with tight domain/range constraints (Feature-of 33.5%, Compare 42.4%) while loose-constraint relations show near-zero violation (Used-for 0.8%).\n25\t\n26\t**Key insight**: Violation rate is driven by **constraint tightness**, not ontology size. A small ontology with tight constraints can produce more violations than a large ontology with loose constraints.\n27\t\n28\t**D014 修订**: DR reduction ceiling 由 **tightness × model RV baseline** 共同决定，非 tightness 单因素。Llama DocRED DR↓90.2% vs Qwen DR↓44.7%（同一 ontology τ̄=0.842）。机制：Qwen RV=29.66% >> Llama RV=16.03% → grammar 层将 OOV triples 强制匹配有效关系名 → 揭露大量 latent DR violations → 残余 DR 更高。这是比单一 tightness 更深的 insight。\n29\t\n30\t**Evidence**: SciERC (7 relations) 15.4%; DocRED (96 relations) 18.7% — comparable rates despite 14× ontology size difference. Schema-informed prompt on DocRED only achieves DR↓32% (vs SciERC ↓62%), confirming **prompt-level intervention scales poorly with ontology complexity**.\n31\t\n32\t### Claim 2 (Empirical): Prompt Insufficiency\n33\tSchema-informed prompting (explicitly describing domain/range constraints in the prompt) reduces but does not eliminate violations:\n34\t- Overall: 15.4% → 5.78% (-62.4%), still above 5%\n35\t- Per-relation: Compare 42.4% → 27.6%, Evaluate-for 24.1% → 29.9% (**worse**)\n36\t- Prompt intervention is unreliable at the per-relation level — some relations improve, one regresses\n37\t\n38\t**Narrative**: This is NOT about \"5.78% barely above 5%\". The story is: **prompt-level intervention is fundamentally unreliable as a guarantee mechanism**. It works statistically but cannot provide per-instance compliance. Three specific relation types retain >10% violation rates with schema-informed prompts. For safety-critical IE (biomedical, legal, regulatory), statistical reduction is insufficient — guaranteed compliance is required.\n39\t\n40\t### Claim 3 (Methodological): Composable Constraint Framework\n41\tOntoCoDec automatically compiles IE ontology schemas into two composable constraint layers:\n42\t1. **Grammar layer** (XGrammar): JSON structure + type vocabulary constraints (CFG-expressible)\n43\t2. **Semantic layer** (TypeConstraintProcessor): Cross-field domain/range constraints via stateful entity registry + dynamic logit masking\n44\t\n45\tThe two layers are **complementary with enabling dependency**: grammar ensures every generated relation type is in the valid vocabulary, which enables the semantic layer to look up and enforce domain/range rules for that type. Without grammar, the semantic layer encounters unknown relation types and cannot enforce constraints (explaining why semantic_only achieves only ↓24% vs full_s1 ↓94%). This is NOT \"synergistic\" (mutual amplification) — grammar is a prerequisite for semantic, not vice versa.\n46\t\n47\tThe two layers compose via bitwise AND of token masks. Recommended framing: \"Grammar and semantic constraints compose via bitwise AND with an enabling dependency: grammar ensures structural validity, enabling semantic constraints to enforce domain/range rules. When constraint tightness creates empty intersection between layers, the system degrades gracefully to grammar-only constraints, maintaining structural validity as a guaranteed floor.\"\n48\t\n49\t**Graceful degradation + Fallback 频率量化** (D008 + Reviewer 发现):\n50\tWhen $M_{semantic} \\cap M_{grammar} = \\emptyset$, the system falls back to grammar-only control.\n51\t\n52\t**关键量化数据（Reviewer 从日志挖掘）**:\n53\t- Llama DocRED full_s1: **32,921 次 fallback / 577 docs = ~57 次/doc**\n54\t- Llama SciERC full_s1: **5,882 次 fallback / 550 docs = ~10.7 次/doc**\n55\t- DocRED fallback 频率是 SciERC 的 **5.3×**\n56\t- Qwen DocRED fallback 率未知（日志当时无 fallback logging，需估算）\n57\t\n58\t**这直接解释了 DocRED DR 残余 10.19% vs SciERC 0.93%**: 更多 token 位置退化为 grammar-only → grammar-only 的 DR 已知为 26.17% → 高 fallback = 高残余 DR。\n59\t\n60\t**论文建议**: 在 §5 tightness 段报告 fallback 率，定义 \"Constraint Coverage\" 指标（semantic masking 实际生效的 token 比例）。这把 \"10.19% DR 残余\" 从弱点变成可量化分析的 finding。Frame as \"engineering robustness\" in §4; fallback 频率 + tightness 作为 §5 定量分析。\n61\t\n62\t**Decidability taxonomy**: Constraints classified by prefix-decidability:\n63\t- (a) Purely local: entity type ∈ vocabulary (grammar layer)\n64\t- (b) Prefix-decidable with state: relation argument types compatible with domain/range (semantic layer, requires entity registry)\n65\t- (c) Truly non-local: forward coreference — out of scope for forward-only decoding\n66\t\n67\t### Claim 4 (Methodological): S1 vs S2 Decoding Strategies — Architectural Ablation\n68\t- S1 (single-pass): Both layers applied throughout generation. **Recommended primary strategy** — simpler, slightly better metrics across the board.\n69\t- S2 (two-pass): Pass 1 extracts entities (grammar-only), Pass 2 generates relations with input-dependent grammar compiled from Pass 1 entities.\n70\t\n71\t**S2 full results (551/551 SciERC)**: DR 0.97% (vs S1 0.93%), CF 8.03% (vs S1 9.9%), R-F1 8.03% (vs S1 8.36%). S2 does NOT solve CF — the 1.87pp reduction is not significant. S2 also slightly worse on DR and F1. **S2 is an architectural variant demonstrating framework flexibility, not a CF solution.** Position in paper as ablation (Section 5 or Appendix), not as a core contribution.\n72\t\n73\t⚠️ **Do NOT cite pilot50 DR=0% as S2 evidence** — small-sample artifact; full run shows DR=0.97%. Per-relation S2 DR is worse than S1 on Compare (4.6% vs 2.82%), Part-of (1.25% vs 0%), Used-for (0.12% vs 0%).\n74\t\n75\t### Claim 5 (Empirical): Cross-Task Generalization — Event Extraction (D040, NEW)\n76\t**Status**: ✅ All 3 models × 246 docs complete (v3 with collision fix + exact-match fix)\n77\t\n78\tOntoCoDec generalizes beyond Relation Extraction to **Event Extraction** (WikiEvents, Li et al. NAACL 2021), demonstrating that the framework is task-agnostic for any IE task with ontology-defined type constraints.\n79\t\n80\t**Cross-task framing (Reviewer 评估 confirmed)**:\n81\t- **RoV 是 DR 的正确对应物**（不是 RV）：EE 中 per-type violation rate 是 RE 的 3-5×，支持 \"more complex ontology → more critical constraint enforcement\" claim\n82\t- **三层级联 Grammar→RoV→AC**（比 RE 的 Grammar→DR 两层更丰富）：grammar 消除 EV，使 semantic layer 可以 enforce role restriction (RoV→0%)，进而暴露 AC violations。这强化 architecture contribution 论证。\n83\t- **Semantic layer 是 EE 的唯一防线**：grammar 层对 role vocabulary 无能力，只有 semantic layer + continuation masking 能 enforce per-event-type role constraints\n84\t- **\"Practical value\" 防线**：Arg F1 ≈ 0% 不削弱 claim，因为 (a) mechanism generalization 是 contribution 不是 SOTA performance，(b) FT composability 已在 RE 中证明 high-F1 场景有效\n85\t\n86\t**WikiEvents specifics** (DARPA KAIROS ontology):\n87\t- 56 event types × 80 argument roles × 27 entity types（含 5 个补充 Contact 子类型 + CRM entity type）\n88\t- 245 组显式 (event_type, role) → allowed_entity_types 约束\n89\t- Maps directly to OntoCoDec's semantic layer: argument role type constraints ≡ domain/range constraints\n90\t- 27 entity types（比 ACE05 的 7 个更丰富）→ constraint space 更大，更能展示 semantic layer 价值\n91\t- 99.98% 数据满足约束 → 约束定义是真实有效的\n92\t- Hierarchical event names (e.g., Conflict.Attack.DetonateExplode) → 扁平化为 leaf-node 解决 first-token collision（96.1%→3.9%）\n93\t\n94\t**数据集选择理由**（MAVEN/RAMS 排除）：\n95\t- MAVEN (168 types): 无 argument extraction，不适用\n96\t- MAVEN-Arg (162 types): FrameNet-based，无 role→entity_type schema 约束\n97\t- RAMS (139 types): 仅 cardinality 约束，无 entity type binding\n98\t- ACE05 (33 types): LDC 付费，采购周期来不及\n99\t- **WikiEvents 是唯一同时满足 \"免费 + 有显式 role→entity_type 约束\" 的数据集**\n100\t\n101\t**Violation 分类** (5 类，从 RE 的 4 类扩展):\n102\t- ET (Entity Type): entity type 不在 ontology 合法类型列表中\n103\t- EV (Event Vocabulary): event type 不在 ontology 定义中\n104\t- RoV (Role Vocabulary): argument role 不在该 event type 定义中\n105\t- AC (Argument Constraint): argument entity type 不满足 role→entity_type 约束（DR 的自然推广）\n106\t- CF (Cross-Field): 同一 entity 跨 event 被赋予不同 type\n107\t\n108\t**Full results (246 docs, v3 final — collision fix + exact-match fix)**:\n109\t\n110\t| Metric | Qwen3-8B uncon. | Qwen3-8B Full S1 | Llama-3.1-8B uncon. | Llama-3.1-8B Full S1 | Mistral-7B uncon. | Mistral-7B Full S1 |\n111\t|--------|-----------------|-------------------|---------------------|----------------------|-------------------|---------------------|\n112\t| Parse | 88.6% | 83.7% | 91.9% | 84.1% | 88.6% | 88.6% |\n113\t| EV | 24.0% | **0%** | 10.5% | **0%** | 37.3% | **0%** |\n114\t| RoV | 74.9% | **0%** | 88.8% | **0%** | 63.9% | **0%** |\n115\t| AC | 0.3% | 2.1% | 0.1% | 3.8% | 0% | 1.3% |\n116\t| CF | 0% | 21.1% | 0% | 17.2% | 0% | 14.9% |\n117\t| Trigger F1 | 11.8% | 13.4% | 5.7% | 7.5% | 2.4% | 3.9% |\n118\t| Ent F1 | 0% | 14.1% | 0% | 17.6% | 0% | 11.7% |\n119\t\n120\t**Grammar-only ablation (Mistral v3, all 3 models)**:\n121\t- Grammar eliminates EV→0% but RoV remains 64-77%: grammar CFG cannot constrain 80 argument roles conditioned on event context\n122\t- AC rises to 8-14% under grammar-only (latent violation surfacing pattern, same as DocRED RE)\n123\t- Proves semantic layer is essential for EE: two-layer architecture is necessary, not just convenient\n124\t\n125\t**Post-hoc filtering comparison (devastating)**:\n126\t- Qwen: 5,467→23 arguments (99.6% discarded) to reach 0% violation\n127\t- Llama: 5,053→3 arguments (99.9% discarded)\n128\t- Mistral: 6,034→0 arguments (100% discarded)\n129\t- Post-hoc is not viable for EE (contrasts with RE where it's expensive but functional)\n130\t\n131\t**BPE collision diagnostic (confirmed 2026-05-18)**:\n132\t- Qwen (BPE, ~152K vocab): **0 collision groups** — all 27 entity types have unique first tokens\n133\t- Llama (BPE, ~128K vocab): **0 collision groups** — same\n134\t- Mistral (SentencePiece, ~32K vocab): **2 collision groups** (SID/SEN/SIDE→'S', BAL/BOD→'B')\n135\t- **Residual AC narrative**: Mistral AC 1.3% = residual after collision fix (was 16.6%); Qwen/Llama AC 2.1-3.8% = purely model semantic confusion (confuses similar entity types like SID vs SEN), NOT tokenizer collision\n136\t\n137\t**关键 findings**:\n138\t- RoV 是压倒性违规（64-89%），远超 RE 的 RV（1-30%）→ 更强力展示 constraint 需求\n139\t- EV 显著（10-37%）→ grammar 层直接消除\n140\t- **Entity F1 从 0% 恢复到 11.7-17.6%**: 不是语义改进，是 format compliance 恢复——grammar enforcement 产生 schema-valid JSON，parser 才能识别 entity mentions\n141\t- Trigger F1 +1.5 to +1.8pp: elimination of OOV event types counted as FP\n142\t- CF 15-21% 比 RE 更高（EE argument structure 更复杂），沿用 RE 的 CF tradeoff framing\n143\t\n144\t**Story upgrade**: WikiEvents results confirm paper narrative: \"universal ontology-constrained structured generation framework applicable to any IE task with formal type constraints\". Three evidence lines: (1) EV/RoV→0% across all models, (2) grammar-only ablation proves two-layer necessity, (3) post-hoc filtering is non-viable for EE. This is the key differentiator for conference main vs Findings.\n145\t\n146\t**70B scale experiment** (P029-P030, in progress): Qwen3-70B AWQ-INT4 on SciERC + DocRED to demonstrate scale generalization. If successful, adds a 4th model to cross-model evidence, strengthening C5.\n147\t\n148\t**Remaining risk**:\n149\t- CF 15-21% higher than RE → continues CF tradeoff framing\n150\t- 70B experiment timeline tight (need results by May 20 for paper integration)\n151\t\n152\t## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n153\t\n154\t### C1: \"5.78% is barely above 5% — threshold is arbitrary\"\n155\t**Response**: Don't argue about the threshold. Argue about per-relation distribution: Compare (27.6%), Evaluate-for (29.9%), Feature-of (11.3%) have double-digit violation rates with schema-informed prompt. The value proposition is per-relation guaranteed compliance, not overall statistical rate.\n156\t\n157\t### C2: \"Why not just post-hoc filter?\"\n158\t**Response (D013, 实验结果已出)**:\n159\t\n160\tPost-hoc filtering 实验结果：post-hoc F1 > OntoCoDec F1（SciERC 8.63 vs 8.36, DocRED 9.61 vs 8.24）——因 low F1 regime 下移除 FP 大幅提升 precision。\n161\t\n162\t**论文 framing（不以 F1 论高低，多维对比）**:\n163\t1. **Recall 维度（核心论点）**: OntoCoDec recall 上升 (SciERC +0.20pp, DocRED +0.56pp) = 概率质量重分配到合法 token 生效。Post-hoc recall 下降 (SciERC -0.72pp, DocRED -1.06pp) = 正确 triple 被误删。\n164\t2. **Information coverage**: DocRED post-hoc 丢弃 **48.1%** triples（近半数信息丢失），SciERC 16.8%。OntoCoDec 保留全部 triple slots。\n165\t3. **Operational**: OntoCoDec 产出即合规、无需后处理、支持流式。Post-hoc 需额外管线、不适用实时场景。\n166\t4. **Precision trade-off（诚实承认）**: \"Post-hoc achieves higher precision by removing a large fraction of triples, many of which are incorrect. This trades information coverage for precision — valid when FP are costly, but inadequate when completeness matters.\"\n167\t\n168\t数据表：SciERC post-hoc rejection 16.8%, OntoCoDec recall 11.60 vs post-hoc 10.68; DocRED post-hoc rejection 48.1%, OntoCoDec recall 10.02 vs post-hoc 8.40。\n169\t\n170\t**Reviewer 补充发现（D013 后）**:\n171\t5. **ET 残余**：post-hoc 只删 triples 不改 entity list，残余 ET=0.4% (SciERC) / 2.47% (DocRED)。OntoCoDec ET=0%。Post-hoc 无法解决 entity type 违规。\n172\t6. **127 个被删 TP (DocRED)**：过滤前 TP=1137，过滤后 TP=1010。丢失的 127 个 TP（11.2%）是正确提取但 entity type 违规的 triple。OntoCoDec 通过生成时强制合法 type 保留这些 TP——\"prevent vs detect\" 核心论据的具体数据。\n173\t7. **OntoCoDec+post-hoc 组合**（future work idea）：先 constrain 再 filter 残余 DR。低优先级，May 19 前不做。\n174\t\n175\t### C3: \"Bitwise AND of two masks is not novel\"\n176\t**Response**: The novelty is not the AND operation — it's (a) the automatic compilation from ontology definitions (zero-code schema compliance), (b) the stateful entity registry enabling cross-field constraints during autoregressive generation, (c) the decidability taxonomy providing theoretical guidance, and (d) the systematic violation landscape measurement motivating the approach.\n177\t\n178\t### C4: \"Evaluate-for violation rate increases with schema-informed prompt\"\n179\t**Response (prior-constraint conflict framework)**: Evaluate-for has 23/36 valid pairs; Method→Task is invalid for Evaluate-for but natural in the LLM's distributional prior (\"Method X evaluates for Task Y\" is semantically plausible). Schema-informed prompting creates a **prior-constraint conflict**: the model learns to avoid Method→Task for Evaluate-for (reducing count 133→87, -34.6%), but the remaining instances are harder boundary cases where the model's type assignment strategy becomes less stable. This is not just \"harder instances\" — it's an active interference between prompt-level constraint signals and the model's learned type associations.\n180\t\n181\t**This strengthens the paper's claim**: prompt-level intervention is not merely insufficient but potentially **counterproductive** for specific constraint configurations. Decoding-time enforcement avoids this issue entirely — it operates on logits, not on the model's reasoning process, so there is no prior-constraint conflict.\n182\t\n183\t### C5: \"Only tested on one model (Qwen3-8B)\"\n184\t**Response**: Cross-model validation DONE (D016 bootstrap verified). Llama-3.1-8B 零代码修改：\n185\t- SciERC: DR 13.34%→0.08% (↓99.4%), R-F1 -0.14pp (p=0.011, negligible), E-F1 NS\n186\t- DocRED: DR 26.07%→2.55% (↓90.2%), R-F1 +0.29pp (p=0.013, significant), E-F1 -0.64pp (p=0.022, modest decline)\n187\t- Parse failures: unconstrained 68 vs full_s1 91 (6.8% vs 9.1%)\n188\t\n189\t**Cross-model claim 指导（Reviewer 专项评估）**:\n190\t- ✅ 可声明：\"OntoCoDec generalizes across model families without code modification\"（程序性事实，铁证）\n191\t- ❌ 不可声明：\"consistently achieves the same reduction rate\"（仅 2 模型，不足以量化声明）\n192\t- **RV↓DR↑ 正交性 finding**: Llama RV baseline 低(16%) 但 DR baseline 高(26%)，反向于 Qwen。证明两层约束解决正交 failure modes——vocabulary compliance ≠ semantic compliance。应作为 §5 cross-model 独立 finding 展开。\n193\t- **Parse failure 偏差**: checker skip parse failures (不计入 F1)，Llama 68/998=6.8% vs Qwen 12/998=1.2%。偏差方向保守（不利于 constrained），不威胁 claim。但需 footnote 披露 + cross-model 表增加 parse failure rate 行。\n194\t- **Llama SciERC CF=6.56%**: 比 Qwen 同量级更高，non-local constraint 问题在 Llama 上更突出，limitations 提及。\n195\t- 等 llama_docred_full_s1 出来后定最终 claim 措辞。\n196\t\n197\t### C6: \"Constrained decoding degrades generation quality (CRANE, Structure Snowballing)\"\n198\t**Response**: OntoCoDec's semantic constraints are narrower than full grammar constraints — only type tokens are masked, free text is unconstrained. **Bootstrap CI (10000×, D012 Qwen + D016 Llama, all registry-aligned)**:\n199\t\n200\t**Qwen3-8B**: SciERC R-F1 +0.13pp (p=0.58, NS), E-F1 -0.03pp (NS). DocRED R-F1 +0.50pp (p<0.001), E-F1 +1.23pp (p<0.001).\n201\t**Llama-3.1-8B**: SciERC R-F1 -0.14pp (p=0.011, negligible), E-F1 NS. DocRED R-F1 +0.29pp (p=0.013), E-F1 -0.64pp (p=0.022).\n202\t\n203\t**Cross-model pattern**: DocRED R-F1 显著提升（两个模型）。E-F1 model-dependent（Qwen +1.23pp, Llama -0.64pp）。\n204\t- 机制：grammar 消除 OOV relation names + 非标 entity types → all_set 方法下减少 FP → precision 提升。Grammar 是 F1 提升的唯一来源（grammar_only Ent F1=59.38% ≈ full_s1 59.37%, Δ=0.01pp, p=0.66）。Semantic 层对 F1 无额外贡献。\n205\t- Frame as: \"On DocRED, R-F1 gains are significant for both models. Entity F1 impact is model-dependent.\"\n206\t- 不升级为 core claim，但如实报告。\n207\t\n208\t### C7: \"Your method trades DR violations for CF violations (cross-field consistency)\"\n209\t**Response**: Both S1 and S2 show elevated CF (per-triple rate ~8-10%). This is an inherent limitation of per-relation independent type enforcement. Must be proactively reported as a limitation. Defense:\n210\t\n211\t**CF 子类型分析（根因已确认）**：\n212\t- **EVR（entity-vs-relation type drift）**: 占 CF 的 >90%。同一 entity 在 entity list 和 relation triple 中被赋予不同 type。S1: 245 entities (7.34%), S2: 178 entities (5.54%, -27%)\n213\t- **Within-rel（同 entity 跨 relation type 不一致）**: S1: 10 (0.36%), S2: 18 (0.72%)\n214\t- S2 减少 EVR 但增加 within-rel——trade-off 更复杂，不是单纯好/差\n215\t\n216\t**Top 冲突模式**: Generic↔OtherScientificTerm (60次), Material↔OtherScientificTerm (28次), Material↔Method (20次)。**这些是 SciERC type system 固有的语义边界模糊区**——同一术语在不同学术语境下确实可以被合理归类为不同 type。CF 在相当程度上是 type system 模糊性的体现，非纯粹的方法缺陷。\n217\t\n218\t**论证层次**：\n219\t1. DR violations = structurally invalid triples（下游系统不可用）→ hard constraint\n220\t2. CF violations = same entity gets different types across relations → individual triples remain type-valid, only cross-triple consistency broken → soft preference\n221\t3. CF 的根因是 type system 语义边界模糊 + per-relation 独立 enforcement，非 bug\n222\t4. Future work: cross-relation global consistency pass (entity-level type consensus before relation-specific enforcement)\n223\t\n224\t**机制归因（口径对账确认）**：grammar_only CF=0.08%（与 unconstrained 持平），full_s1 CF=9.90%，full_s2 CF=8.03%。**CF 100% 由 semantic 层引入，grammar 层无贡献。** 这为 \"CF 是 semantic type enforcement 的系统性副作用\" 提供干净的消融证据。\n225\t\n226\t**论文数字口径**：CF rate 用 violation_checker 口径（denominator=total_entities，与 DR/RV/ET 一致）。分析段落额外给 entity-level EVR 率 + 受影响样本比例。注意：analyze_cf 脚本的 EVR/WR 两维度不是独立的（WR⊂EVR），论文中不要作为两个独立维度报告。\n227\t\n228\t**Do NOT hide this data.** Proactive disclosure + severity distinction + root cause analysis + type ambiguity evidence + 消融归因 = 最强防御策略。\n229\t\n230\t### C8: \"Absolute F1 is too low (~8%) — results are not meaningful\"\n231\t**Response**: This is a zero-shot extraction setting (no training data, no fine-tuning). Low F1 is expected — supervised SOTA on SciERC relation F1 is ~40-50%. Our contribution is the constraint enforcement method, not extraction quality. F1 is a control variable verifying constraints don't degrade quality, not an optimization target. Recommended framing: \"We evaluate in a zero-shot setting to demonstrate that our constraint enforcement method works without task-specific training. F1 is reported to verify that constraint enforcement does not degrade extraction quality, not as a claim of state-of-the-art performance.\"\n232\t\n233\t## Paper Structure (Draft — D040 updated)\n234\t1. Introduction: Ontology constraint violations in LLM-based structured generation + composable framework overview (story: not just RE, general ontology-constrained generation)\n235\t2. Background: Grammar-constrained decoding (XGrammar) + IE ontology structure\n236\t3. Violation Landscape Study (Phase 0 empirics — independent contribution)\n237\t4. OntoCoDec Framework: Compiler + TypeConstraintProcessor + S1/S2 strategies\n238\t5. Experiments:\n239\t   - §5.1-5.3: RE experiments (SciERC + DocRED, 3 models, constrained vs unconstrained vs post-hoc vs prompt-based)\n240\t   - §5.4: **Event Extraction (WikiEvents)** — cross-task generalization (D040)\n241\t   - §5.5: Ablation + analysis (composability, latency, beam search, etc.)\n242\t6. Related Work: 5 constraint paradigms (grammar, vocabulary, structural, type-checking, ontology) + event extraction methods\n243\t7. Conclusion: Framework generality across IE tasks\n244\t\n245\t## Claim Calibration (per Reviewer assessment)\n246\t\n247\t**Safe to claim (sufficient evidence from Phase 2)**:\n248\t- \"First systematic study of ontology constraint violations in LLM-based IE\"\n249\t- \"Violation rate correlates with constraint tightness, not ontology size\" (D014: DR reduction ceiling 由 tightness × model RV baseline 共同决定)\n250\t- \"Grammar+semantic constrained decoding eliminates 94% of DR violations at zero F1 cost\" ✅ Phase 2 confirmed\n251\t- \"Two-layer architecture provides complementary coverage — grammar enables semantic\" ✅ Ablation confirmed\n252\t- \"Prompt-level intervention scales poorly with ontology complexity\" ✅ SciERC ↓62% vs DocRED ↓32%\n253\t\n254\t**Claim with caution**:\n255\t- \"Near-complete type-valid IE\" — S1 0.93%, S2 0.97% residual, not truly 0%. Title updated to \"Near-Complete\"\n256\t- \"Principled framework applicable to arbitrary IE ontologies\" — RE validated on 2 datasets × 2 models; EE (WikiEvents) 10-doc preliminary shows ↓95.8% semantic violations, full results pending\n257\t- \"F1 improvement\" — SciERC: not significant (p=0.58), frame as F1-neutral; DocRED: significant (+0.50pp, p<0.001), 可报告但不升级为 core claim，归因于 OOV elimination 而非约束解码本身的提升\n258\t- \"CF reveals type system ambiguity\" — 可在 §5.3 作为 analysis finding 展开（Generic↔OtherScientificTerm 等模式有独立 insight 价值），但 §7 必须同时保留 CF 作为 limitation + future work。**两处都要有，缺一不可。** 不能暗示\"因为是 type ambiguity 所以 CF 可接受\"\n259\t\n260\t**Do NOT claim**:\n261\t- \"General infrastructure for IE\" — only zero-shot extraction validated\n262\t- \"State-of-the-art\" — F1 is control variable, not optimization target (see C8)\n263\t- \"Synergistic effect\" — mechanism is enabling dependency, not mutual amplification (see Claim 3)\n264\t- \"S2 solves CF\" or \"S2 mitigates Structure Snowballing\" — data shows S2 ≈ S1 on all metrics; position as architectural variant only\n265\t- \"Pilot50 DR=0%\" — small-sample artifact, full S2 has DR=0.97%\n266\t- \"Grammar-first invariant\" 作为独立 claim — 证据不足（仅 1 次崩溃触发，实现是 fallback 非形式化保证）。写入 §4 方法论设计原则（1-2 句），不升级为 claim\n267\t- \"Robust dual-layer composition across schema complexities\" — 等 DocRED 完成。最终如 fallback ≤5/998，可写经验性陈述，不做泛化 claim\n268\t\n269\t## Risk Ranking (ordered by reject probability)\n270\t\n271\t1. **CF violation trade-off under-addressed** (MEDIUM-HIGH): S1 9.9%, S2 8.03% — both elevated. **S2 confirmed: does NOT solve CF.** This is the #1 attack surface. Mitigated by proactive disclosure + severity distinction + root cause analysis (C7). Must be reported as explicit limitation with future work direction (global entity-type consensus).\n272\t2. ~~**Single model limitation**~~ (RESOLVED): Llama-3.1-8B SciERC ✅ (DR↓99.4%) + DocRED ✅ (DR↓90.2%). 2 模型 × 2 数据集全矩阵完成。\n273\t3. **Novelty perception** (MEDIUM): \"PLDI'25 for code → OntoCoDec for IE\" attack line. Must argue IE constraint structure differs fundamentally.\n274\t4. ~~**DocRED Phase 2 weak**~~ (RESOLVED → reframed as D014): Qwen DR↓44.7%, Llama DR↓90.2% — both substantial. Weaker Qwen reduction explained by RV baseline interaction (D014), not method failure.\n275\t5. ~~**Phase 2 F1 drop**~~ (RESOLVED): F1 confirmed neutral (SciERC) or positive (DocRED, p<0.001). Bootstrap CI D012 confirms. No longer a risk.\n276\t\n277\t## Critical Path to EMNLP Submission (May 25)\n278\t\n279\t- **May 13-14**: Phase 0 + Phase 1 + Phase 2 SciERC ✅\n280\t- **May 14**: Phase 2 DocRED 4-way ablation ✅ + Llama SciERC cross-model ✅ + Dream 完成 (3/6)\n281\t- **May 14-15**: Llama DocRED ✅ + Checker 修正 ✅ + post-hoc ✅ + bootstrap CI ✅ + related work ✅\n282\t- **May 15-17**: Prompt sensitivity ✅ + WikiEvents pipeline 开发 + continuation v2 突破\n283\t- **May 17-18**: WikiEvents 3 模型 unconstrained baselines (进行中) + constrained 全量\n284\t- **May 18-19**: WikiEvents 结果分析 + §5.4 Event Extraction 章节撰写\n285\t- **May 19-20**: Intro/Abstract/Conclusion 升级（cross-task story）+ 内部稿 → submit_paper_to_review\n286\t- **May 20-24**: Review 修改 + 最终提交\n287\t\n288\t**当前瓶颈**: WikiEvents 全量实验完成是关键路径。3 模型 unconstrained baselines 并行进行中（Qwen ~68/246, Mistral ~31/246, Llama 重启中），constrained 实验随后立即启动。\n289\t\n290\t## Status\n291\t- Phase 0 SciERC: ✅ Complete (minimal + schema-informed)\n292\t- Phase 0 DocRED: ✅ Complete (minimal 18.7% DR + schema-informed 12.8% DR)\n293\t- Phase 1 Compiler: ✅ Complete (grammar + semantic layers integrated)\n294\t- Phase 2 SciERC (5 configs): ✅ Complete (S1 DR↓94% F1-neutral, S2 降级为 ablation)\n295\t- Phase 2 DocRED (4 configs): ✅ Complete (full_s1 DR↓45%, grammar ET/RV→0%)\n296\t- Llama SciERC cross-model: ✅ Complete (DR↓99.4%, F1-neutral, 零代码修改)\n297\t- Llama DocRED cross-model: ✅ Complete (full_s1 DR↓90.2%, unconstrained DR=26.07%)\n298\t- Checker v2 (D011): ✅ Fixed (ET triple-counting → unique entity dedup)\n299\t- Bootstrap CI (D012): ✅ Fixed + confirmed (entity filter bug resolved)\n300\t- Post-hoc baseline (D013): ✅ Complete (multi-dimensional framing)\n301\t- Related work: ✅ 42 bib entries, 4 additions merged\n302\t- Dream 6/6 actions: ✅ All complete\n303\t- CF violation analysis: ✅ Confirmed inherent limitation (S1 9.9% SciERC / 2.57% DocRED / 12.02% Llama DocRED)\n304\t- D014 tightness revision: ✅ Complete (tightness × RV baseline dual-factor)\n305\t- Llama bootstrap CI (D016): ✅ Fixed + verified (registry-aligned ≤0.05pp, all p-values in paper)\n306\t- Paper compilation: ✅ 8 pages正文 + appendix\n307\t- R5 text fixes (N1/N2/N3/W1-W6): ✅ All complete and verified\n308\t- Prompt sensitivity analysis: ✅ Complete (3 prompts × 2 modes, DR reduction 94.0-94.6%, σ=0.3pp; appendix written)\n309\t- Doc length breakdown: ✅ Complete (appendix written)\n310\t- **WikiEvents Event Extraction (D040)**: 🔄 Continuation v2 突破 (10-doc: RoV 0%, semantic ↓95.8%); 3 模型 unconstrained baselines 进行中; constrained 全量待启动\n311\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1df8b9e0-2dfb-4e94-93b6-aca94befa4d2","uuid":"3b2f88fc-0167-4cab-8d58-204e30ab0a83","timestamp":"2026-05-18T16:56:15.351Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_6/projects/schema_semantic_constrained_ie/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260518T162745/best/paper_framing.md","content":"# OntoCoDec — Paper Framing\n\n## Target Venue\nEMNLP 2026 (ARR submission May 25, 2026) — **目标: conference main**（D040, 用户明确指示）\n\n## Title\nOntoCoDec: Type-Valid Information Extraction via Compiled Ontology Constraints\n(D015: \"Near-Complete\" dropped — DocRED residual DR=10.21% (Qwen) 不算 near-complete。论文贡献是方法，不是特定消除率。SciERC 0.93% 和 DocRED 2.55% (Llama) 可在正文中描述为 near-complete，但 title 不宜 overclaim。)\n\n**D040 Story 升级方向**: 从 \"IE-specific constrained decoding\" → \"universal ontology-constrained structured generation framework\"。WikiEvents Event Extraction 验证跨任务泛化。Continuation masking v2 突破（10-doc: RoV 0%, semantic violations ↓95.8%）初步确认跨任务有效性，全量实验进行中。最终 title 待全量结果后调整。\n\n## Core Insight\nLLM-based IE systems produce systematic ontology constraint violations concentrated in specific relation types. Prompt-level intervention (schema-informed prompting) reduces violations by ~62% but cannot eliminate them — certain relation types retain 25-30% violation rates even with explicit constraint descriptions. OntoCoDec provides **near-complete elimination (DR 15.4%→0.93%, ↓94%) at zero or positive F1 impact** through automatic ontology-to-decoder constraint compilation with two complementary layers.\n\n**Phase 2 confirmed (D012 bootstrap CI, v2 fix)**: Grammar+Semantic dual-layer constrained decoding reduces domain/range violations by 94%, eliminates entity-type and relation-vocabulary violations entirely (→0%). F1 impact is **dataset-dependent**:\n- SciERC: Rel F1 neutral (+0.13pp, p=0.58), Ent F1 neutral (-0.03pp, p=0.53)\n- DocRED: Rel F1 **significantly improved** (+0.50pp, p<0.001, 95% CI [+0.23, +0.81]); Ent F1 **significantly improved** (+1.23pp, p<0.001, 95% CI [+0.94, +1.55])\n- Mechanism: grammar 消除 OOV relation names (DocRED RV 29.66%→0.03%) + 非标 entity types (ET 2.48%→0%)。all_set F1 方法下 OOV=FP → fewer FP → higher precision/F1。SciERC baseline RV/ET 已很低，效果不显著。\n- **Grammar 层是 F1 提升的唯一来源**: grammar_only Ent F1=59.38% ≈ full_s1 59.37% (Δ+0.01pp, p=0.66)。Semantic 层对 F1 无额外贡献，专注 DR reduction。\n\n## Core Claims\n\n### Claim 1 (Empirical): Violation Landscape\nLLM-based IE systems violate ontology type constraints at non-trivial rates (15.4% per-triple on SciERC, 18.7% on DocRED). Violations are **not uniformly distributed** — they concentrate on relation types with tight domain/range constraints (Feature-of 33.5%, Compare 42.4%) while loose-constraint relations show near-zero violation (Used-for 0.8%).\n\n**Key insight**: Violation rate is driven by **constraint tightness**, not ontology size. A small ontology with tight constraints can produce more violations than a large ontology with loose constraints.\n\n**D014 修订**: DR reduction ceiling 由 **tightness × model RV baseline** 共同决定，非 tightness 单因素。Llama DocRED DR↓90.2% vs Qwen DR↓44.7%（同一 ontology τ̄=0.842）。机制：Qwen RV=29.66% >> Llama RV=16.03% → grammar 层将 OOV triples 强制匹配有效关系名 → 揭露大量 latent DR violations → 残余 DR 更高。这是比单一 tightness 更深的 insight。\n\n**Evidence**: SciERC (7 relations) 15.4%; DocRED (96 relations) 18.7% — comparable rates despite 14× ontology size difference. Schema-informed prompt on DocRED only achieves DR↓32% (vs SciERC ↓62%), confirming **prompt-level intervention scales poorly with ontology complexity**.\n\n### Claim 2 (Empirical): Prompt Insufficiency\nSchema-informed prompting (explicitly describing domain/range constraints in the prompt) reduces but does not eliminate violations:\n- Overall: 15.4% → 5.78% (-62.4%), still above 5%\n- Per-relation: Compare 42.4% → 27.6%, Evaluate-for 24.1% → 29.9% (**worse**)\n- Prompt intervention is unreliable at the per-relation level — some relations improve, one regresses\n\n**Narrative**: This is NOT about \"5.78% barely above 5%\". The story is: **prompt-level intervention is fundamentally unreliable as a guarantee mechanism**. It works statistically but cannot provide per-instance compliance. Three specific relation types retain >10% violation rates with schema-informed prompts. For safety-critical IE (biomedical, legal, regulatory), statistical reduction is insufficient — guaranteed compliance is required.\n\n### Claim 3 (Methodological): Composable Constraint Framework\nOntoCoDec automatically compiles IE ontology schemas into two composable constraint layers:\n1. **Grammar layer** (XGrammar): JSON structure + type vocabulary constraints (CFG-expressible)\n2. **Semantic layer** (TypeConstraintProcessor): Cross-field domain/range constraints via stateful entity registry + dynamic logit masking\n\nThe two layers are **complementary with enabling dependency**: grammar ensures every generated relation type is in the valid vocabulary, which enables the semantic layer to look up and enforce domain/range rules for that type. Without grammar, the semantic layer encounters unknown relation types and cannot enforce constraints (explaining why semantic_only achieves only ↓24% vs full_s1 ↓94%). This is NOT \"synergistic\" (mutual amplification) — grammar is a prerequisite for semantic, not vice versa.\n\nThe two layers compose via bitwise AND of token masks. Recommended framing: \"Grammar and semantic constraints compose via bitwise AND with an enabling dependency: grammar ensures structural validity, enabling semantic constraints to enforce domain/range rules. When constraint tightness creates empty intersection between layers, the system degrades gracefully to grammar-only constraints, maintaining structural validity as a guaranteed floor.\"\n\n**Graceful degradation + Fallback 频率量化** (D008 + Reviewer 发现):\nWhen $M_{semantic} \\cap M_{grammar} = \\emptyset$, the system falls back to grammar-only control.\n\n**关键量化数据（Reviewer 从日志挖掘）**:\n- Llama DocRED full_s1: **32,921 次 fallback / 577 docs = ~57 次/doc**\n- Llama SciERC full_s1: **5,882 次 fallback / 550 docs = ~10.7 次/doc**\n- DocRED fallback 频率是 SciERC 的 **5.3×**\n- Qwen DocRED fallback 率未知（日志当时无 fallback logging，需估算）\n\n**这直接解释了 DocRED DR 残余 10.19% vs SciERC 0.93%**: 更多 token 位置退化为 grammar-only → grammar-only 的 DR 已知为 26.17% → 高 fallback = 高残余 DR。\n\n**论文建议**: 在 §5 tightness 段报告 fallback 率，定义 \"Constraint Coverage\" 指标（semantic masking 实际生效的 token 比例）。这把 \"10.19% DR 残余\" 从弱点变成可量化分析的 finding。Frame as \"engineering robustness\" in §4; fallback 频率 + tightness 作为 §5 定量分析。\n\n**Decidability taxonomy**: Constraints classified by prefix-decidability:\n- (a) Purely local: entity type ∈ vocabulary (grammar layer)\n- (b) Prefix-decidable with state: relation argument types compatible with domain/range (semantic layer, requires entity registry)\n- (c) Truly non-local: forward coreference — out of scope for forward-only decoding\n\n### Claim 4 (Methodological): S1 vs S2 Decoding Strategies — Architectural Ablation\n- S1 (single-pass): Both layers applied throughout generation. **Recommended primary strategy** — simpler, slightly better metrics across the board.\n- S2 (two-pass): Pass 1 extracts entities (grammar-only), Pass 2 generates relations with input-dependent grammar compiled from Pass 1 entities.\n\n**S2 full results (551/551 SciERC)**: DR 0.97% (vs S1 0.93%), CF 8.03% (vs S1 9.9%), R-F1 8.03% (vs S1 8.36%). S2 does NOT solve CF — the 1.87pp reduction is not significant. S2 also slightly worse on DR and F1. **S2 is an architectural variant demonstrating framework flexibility, not a CF solution.** Position in paper as ablation (Section 5 or Appendix), not as a core contribution.\n\n⚠️ **Do NOT cite pilot50 DR=0% as S2 evidence** — small-sample artifact; full run shows DR=0.97%. Per-relation S2 DR is worse than S1 on Compare (4.6% vs 2.82%), Part-of (1.25% vs 0%), Used-for (0.12% vs 0%).\n\n### Claim 5 (Empirical): Cross-Task Generalization — Event Extraction (D040, NEW)\n**Status**: ✅ All 3 models × 246 docs complete (v3 with collision fix + exact-match fix)\n\nOntoCoDec generalizes beyond Relation Extraction to **Event Extraction** (WikiEvents, Li et al. NAACL 2021), demonstrating that the framework is task-agnostic for any IE task with ontology-defined type constraints.\n\n**Cross-task framing (Reviewer 评估 confirmed)**:\n- **RoV 是 DR 的正确对应物**（不是 RV）：EE 中 per-type violation rate 是 RE 的 3-5×，支持 \"more complex ontology → more critical constraint enforcement\" claim\n- **三层级联 Grammar→RoV→AC**（比 RE 的 Grammar→DR 两层更丰富）：grammar 消除 EV，使 semantic layer 可以 enforce role restriction (RoV→0%)，进而暴露 AC violations。这强化 architecture contribution 论证。\n- **Semantic layer 是 EE 的唯一防线**：grammar 层对 role vocabulary 无能力，只有 semantic layer + continuation masking 能 enforce per-event-type role constraints\n- **\"Practical value\" 防线**：Arg F1 ≈ 0% 不削弱 claim，因为 (a) mechanism generalization 是 contribution 不是 SOTA performance，(b) FT composability 已在 RE 中证明 high-F1 场景有效\n\n**WikiEvents specifics** (DARPA KAIROS ontology):\n- 56 event types × 80 argument roles × 27 entity types（含 5 个补充 Contact 子类型 + CRM entity type）\n- 245 组显式 (event_type, role) → allowed_entity_types 约束\n- Maps directly to OntoCoDec's semantic layer: argument role type constraints ≡ domain/range constraints\n- 27 entity types（比 ACE05 的 7 个更丰富）→ constraint space 更大，更能展示 semantic layer 价值\n- 99.98% 数据满足约束 → 约束定义是真实有效的\n- Hierarchical event names (e.g., Conflict.Attack.DetonateExplode) → 扁平化为 leaf-node 解决 first-token collision（96.1%→3.9%）\n\n**数据集选择理由**（MAVEN/RAMS 排除）：\n- MAVEN (168 types): 无 argument extraction，不适用\n- MAVEN-Arg (162 types): FrameNet-based，无 role→entity_type schema 约束\n- RAMS (139 types): 仅 cardinality 约束，无 entity type binding\n- ACE05 (33 types): LDC 付费，采购周期来不及\n- **WikiEvents 是唯一同时满足 \"免费 + 有显式 role→entity_type 约束\" 的数据集**\n\n**Violation 分类** (5 类，从 RE 的 4 类扩展):\n- ET (Entity Type): entity type 不在 ontology 合法类型列表中\n- EV (Event Vocabulary): event type 不在 ontology 定义中\n- RoV (Role Vocabulary): argument role 不在该 event type 定义中\n- AC (Argument Constraint): argument entity type 不满足 role→entity_type 约束（DR 的自然推广）\n- CF (Cross-Field): 同一 entity 跨 event 被赋予不同 type\n\n**Full results (246 docs, v3 final — collision fix + exact-match fix)**:\n\n| Metric | Qwen3-8B uncon. | Qwen3-8B Full S1 | Llama-3.1-8B uncon. | Llama-3.1-8B Full S1 | Mistral-7B uncon. | Mistral-7B Full S1 |\n|--------|-----------------|-------------------|---------------------|----------------------|-------------------|---------------------|\n| Parse | 88.6% | 83.7% | 91.9% | 84.1% | 88.6% | 88.6% |\n| EV | 24.0% | **0%** | 10.5% | **0%** | 37.3% | **0%** |\n| RoV | 74.9% | **0%** | 88.8% | **0%** | 63.9% | **0%** |\n| AC | 0.3% | 2.1% | 0.1% | 3.8% | 0% | 1.3% |\n| CF | 0% | 21.1% | 0% | 17.2% | 0% | 14.9% |\n| Trigger F1 | 11.8% | 13.4% | 5.7% | 7.5% | 2.4% | 3.9% |\n| Ent F1 | 0% | 14.1% | 0% | 17.6% | 0% | 11.7% |\n\n**Grammar-only ablation (Mistral v3, all 3 models)**:\n- Grammar eliminates EV→0% but RoV remains 64-77%: grammar CFG cannot constrain 80 argument roles conditioned on event context\n- AC rises to 8-14% under grammar-only (latent violation surfacing pattern, same as DocRED RE)\n- Proves semantic layer is essential for EE: two-layer architecture is necessary, not just convenient\n\n**Post-hoc filtering comparison (devastating)**:\n- Qwen: 5,467→23 arguments (99.6% discarded) to reach 0% violation\n- Llama: 5,053→3 arguments (99.9% discarded)\n- Mistral: 6,034→0 arguments (100% discarded)\n- Post-hoc is not viable for EE (contrasts with RE where it's expensive but functional)\n\n**BPE collision diagnostic (confirmed 2026-05-18)**:\n- Qwen (BPE, ~152K vocab): **0 collision groups** — all 27 entity types have unique first tokens\n- Llama (BPE, ~128K vocab): **0 collision groups** — same\n- Mistral (SentencePiece, ~32K vocab): **2 collision groups** (SID/SEN/SIDE→'S', BAL/BOD→'B')\n- **Residual AC narrative**: Mistral AC 1.3% = residual after collision fix (was 16.6%); Qwen/Llama AC 2.1-3.8% = purely model semantic confusion (confuses similar entity types like SID vs SEN), NOT tokenizer collision\n\n**关键 findings**:\n- RoV 是压倒性违规（64-89%），远超 RE 的 RV（1-30%）→ 更强力展示 constraint 需求\n- EV 显著（10-37%）→ grammar 层直接消除\n- **Entity F1 从 0% 恢复到 11.7-17.6%**: 不是语义改进，是 format compliance 恢复——grammar enforcement 产生 schema-valid JSON，parser 才能识别 entity mentions\n- Trigger F1 +1.5 to +1.8pp: elimination of OOV event types counted as FP\n- CF 15-21% 比 RE 更高（EE argument structure 更复杂），沿用 RE 的 CF tradeoff framing\n\n**Story upgrade**: WikiEvents results confirm paper narrative: \"universal ontology-constrained structured generation framework applicable to any IE task with formal type constraints\". Three evidence lines: (1) EV/RoV→0% across all models, (2) grammar-only ablation proves two-layer necessity, (3) post-hoc filtering is non-viable for EE. This is the key differentiator for conference main vs Findings.\n\n**70B scale experiment** (P029-P030, in progress): Qwen3-70B AWQ-INT4 on SciERC + DocRED to demonstrate scale generalization. If successful, adds a 4th model to cross-model evidence, strengthening C5.\n\n**Remaining risk**:\n- CF 15-21% higher than RE → continues CF tradeoff framing\n- 70B experiment timeline tight (need results by May 20 for paper integration)\n\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n\n### C1: \"5.78% is barely above 5% — threshold is arbitrary\"\n**Response**: Don't argue about the threshold. Argue about per-relation distribution: Compare (27.6%), Evaluate-for (29.9%), Feature-of (11.3%) have double-digit violation rates with schema-informed prompt. The value proposition is per-relation guaranteed compliance, not overall statistical rate.\n\n### C2: \"Why not just post-hoc filter?\"\n**Response (D013, 实验结果已出)**:\n\nPost-hoc filtering 实验结果：post-hoc F1 > OntoCoDec F1（SciERC 8.63 vs 8.36, DocRED 9.61 vs 8.24）——因 low F1 regime 下移除 FP 大幅提升 precision。\n\n**论文 framing（不以 F1 论高低，多维对比）**:\n1. **Recall 维度（核心论点）**: OntoCoDec recall 上升 (SciERC +0.20pp, DocRED +0.56pp) = 概率质量重分配到合法 token 生效。Post-hoc recall 下降 (SciERC -0.72pp, DocRED -1.06pp) = 正确 triple 被误删。\n2. **Information coverage**: DocRED post-hoc 丢弃 **48.1%** triples（近半数信息丢失），SciERC 16.8%。OntoCoDec 保留全部 triple slots。\n3. **Operational**: OntoCoDec 产出即合规、无需后处理、支持流式。Post-hoc 需额外管线、不适用实时场景。\n4. **Precision trade-off（诚实承认）**: \"Post-hoc achieves higher precision by removing a large fraction of triples, many of which are incorrect. This trades information coverage for precision — valid when FP are costly, but inadequate when completeness matters.\"\n\n数据表：SciERC post-hoc rejection 16.8%, OntoCoDec recall 11.60 vs post-hoc 10.68; DocRED post-hoc rejection 48.1%, OntoCoDec recall 10.02 vs post-hoc 8.40。\n\n**Reviewer 补充发现（D013 后）**:\n5. **ET 残余**：post-hoc 只删 triples 不改 entity list，残余 ET=0.4% (SciERC) / 2.47% (DocRED)。OntoCoDec ET=0%。Post-hoc 无法解决 entity type 违规。\n6. **127 个被删 TP (DocRED)**：过滤前 TP=1137，过滤后 TP=1010。丢失的 127 个 TP（11.2%）是正确提取但 entity type 违规的 triple。OntoCoDec 通过生成时强制合法 type 保留这些 TP——\"prevent vs detect\" 核心论据的具体数据。\n7. **OntoCoDec+post-hoc 组合**（future work idea）：先 constrain 再 filter 残余 DR。低优先级，May 19 前不做。\n\n### C3: \"Bitwise AND of two masks is not novel\"\n**Response**: The novelty is not the AND operation — it's (a) the automatic compilation from ontology definitions (zero-code schema compliance), (b) the stateful entity registry enabling cross-field constraints during autoregressive generation, (c) the decidability taxonomy providing theoretical guidance, and (d) the systematic violation landscape measurement motivating the approach.\n\n### C4: \"Evaluate-for violation rate increases with schema-informed prompt\"\n**Response (prior-constraint conflict framework)**: Evaluate-for has 23/36 valid pairs; Method→Task is invalid for Evaluate-for but natural in the LLM's distributional prior (\"Method X evaluates for Task Y\" is semantically plausible). Schema-informed prompting creates a **prior-constraint conflict**: the model learns to avoid Method→Task for Evaluate-for (reducing count 133→87, -34.6%), but the remaining instances are harder boundary cases where the model's type assignment strategy becomes less stable. This is not just \"harder instances\" — it's an active interference between prompt-level constraint signals and the model's learned type associations.\n\n**This strengthens the paper's claim**: prompt-level intervention is not merely insufficient but potentially **counterproductive** for specific constraint configurations. Decoding-time enforcement avoids this issue entirely — it operates on logits, not on the model's reasoning process, so there is no prior-constraint conflict.\n\n### C5: \"Only tested on one model (Qwen3-8B)\"\n**Response**: Cross-model validation DONE (D016 bootstrap verified). Llama-3.1-8B 零代码修改：\n- SciERC: DR 13.34%→0.08% (↓99.4%), R-F1 -0.14pp (p=0.011, negligible), E-F1 NS\n- DocRED: DR 26.07%→2.55% (↓90.2%), R-F1 +0.29pp (p=0.013, significant), E-F1 -0.64pp (p=0.022, modest decline)\n- Parse failures: unconstrained 68 vs full_s1 91 (6.8% vs 9.1%)\n\n**Cross-model claim 指导（Reviewer 专项评估）**:\n- ✅ 可声明：\"OntoCoDec generalizes across model families without code modification\"（程序性事实，铁证）\n- ❌ 不可声明：\"consistently achieves the same reduction rate\"（仅 2 模型，不足以量化声明）\n- **RV↓DR↑ 正交性 finding**: Llama RV baseline 低(16%) 但 DR baseline 高(26%)，反向于 Qwen。证明两层约束解决正交 failure modes——vocabulary compliance ≠ semantic compliance。应作为 §5 cross-model 独立 finding 展开。\n- **Parse failure 偏差**: checker skip parse failures (不计入 F1)，Llama 68/998=6.8% vs Qwen 12/998=1.2%。偏差方向保守（不利于 constrained），不威胁 claim。但需 footnote 披露 + cross-model 表增加 parse failure rate 行。\n- **Llama SciERC CF=6.56%**: 比 Qwen 同量级更高，non-local constraint 问题在 Llama 上更突出，limitations 提及。\n- 等 llama_docred_full_s1 出来后定最终 claim 措辞。\n\n### C6: \"Constrained decoding degrades generation quality (CRANE, Structure Snowballing)\"\n**Response**: OntoCoDec's semantic constraints are narrower than full grammar constraints — only type tokens are masked, free text is unconstrained. **Bootstrap CI (10000×, D012 Qwen + D016 Llama, all registry-aligned)**:\n\n**Qwen3-8B**: SciERC R-F1 +0.13pp (p=0.58, NS), E-F1 -0.03pp (NS). DocRED R-F1 +0.50pp (p<0.001), E-F1 +1.23pp (p<0.001).\n**Llama-3.1-8B**: SciERC R-F1 -0.14pp (p=0.011, negligible), E-F1 NS. DocRED R-F1 +0.29pp (p=0.013), E-F1 -0.64pp (p=0.022).\n\n**Cross-model pattern**: DocRED R-F1 显著提升（两个模型）。E-F1 model-dependent（Qwen +1.23pp, Llama -0.64pp）。\n- 机制：grammar 消除 OOV relation names + 非标 entity types → all_set 方法下减少 FP → precision 提升。Grammar 是 F1 提升的唯一来源（grammar_only Ent F1=59.38% ≈ full_s1 59.37%, Δ=0.01pp, p=0.66）。Semantic 层对 F1 无额外贡献。\n- Frame as: \"On DocRED, R-F1 gains are significant for both models. Entity F1 impact is model-dependent.\"\n- 不升级为 core claim，但如实报告。\n\n### C7: \"Your method trades DR violations for CF violations (cross-field consistency)\"\n**Response**: Both S1 and S2 show elevated CF (per-triple rate ~8-10%). This is an inherent limitation of per-relation independent type enforcement. Must be proactively reported as a limitation. Defense:\n\n**CF 子类型分析（根因已确认）**：\n- **EVR（entity-vs-relation type drift）**: 占 CF 的 >90%。同一 entity 在 entity list 和 relation triple 中被赋予不同 type。S1: 245 entities (7.34%), S2: 178 entities (5.54%, -27%)\n- **Within-rel（同 entity 跨 relation type 不一致）**: S1: 10 (0.36%), S2: 18 (0.72%)\n- S2 减少 EVR 但增加 within-rel——trade-off 更复杂，不是单纯好/差\n\n**Top 冲突模式**: Generic↔OtherScientificTerm (60次), Material↔OtherScientificTerm (28次), Material↔Method (20次)。**这些是 SciERC type system 固有的语义边界模糊区**——同一术语在不同学术语境下确实可以被合理归类为不同 type。CF 在相当程度上是 type system 模糊性的体现，非纯粹的方法缺陷。\n\n**论证层次**：\n1. DR violations = structurally invalid triples（下游系统不可用）→ hard constraint\n2. CF violations = same entity gets different types across relations → individual triples remain type-valid, only cross-triple consistency broken → soft preference\n3. CF 的根因是 type system 语义边界模糊 + per-relation 独立 enforcement，非 bug\n4. Future work: cross-relation global consistency pass (entity-level type consensus before relation-specific enforcement)\n\n**机制归因（口径对账确认）**：grammar_only CF=0.08%（与 unconstrained 持平），full_s1 CF=9.90%，full_s2 CF=8.03%。**CF 100% 由 semantic 层引入，grammar 层无贡献。** 这为 \"CF 是 semantic type enforcement 的系统性副作用\" 提供干净的消融证据。\n\n**论文数字口径**：CF rate 用 violation_checker 口径（denominator=total_entities，与 DR/RV/ET 一致）。分析段落额外给 entity-level EVR 率 + 受影响样本比例。注意：analyze_cf 脚本的 EVR/WR 两维度不是独立的（WR⊂EVR），论文中不要作为两个独立维度报告。\n\n**Do NOT hide this data.** Proactive disclosure + severity distinction + root cause analysis + type ambiguity evidence + 消融归因 = 最强防御策略。\n\n### C8: \"Absolute F1 is too low (~8%) — results are not meaningful\"\n**Response**: This is a zero-shot extraction setting (no training data, no fine-tuning). Low F1 is expected — supervised SOTA on SciERC relation F1 is ~40-50%. Our contribution is the constraint enforcement method, not extraction quality. F1 is a control variable verifying constraints don't degrade quality, not an optimization target. Recommended framing: \"We evaluate in a zero-shot setting to demonstrate that our constraint enforcement method works without task-specific training. F1 is reported to verify that constraint enforcement does not degrade extraction quality, not as a claim of state-of-the-art performance.\"\n\n## Paper Structure (Draft — D040 updated)\n1. Introduction: Ontology constraint violations in LLM-based structured generation + composable framework overview (story: not just RE, general ontology-constrained generation)\n2. Background: Grammar-constrained decoding (XGrammar) + IE ontology structure\n3. Violation Landscape Study (Phase 0 empirics — independent contribution)\n4. OntoCoDec Framework: Compiler + TypeConstraintProcessor + S1/S2 strategies\n5. Experiments:\n   - §5.1-5.3: RE experiments (SciERC + DocRED, 3 models, constrained vs unconstrained vs post-hoc vs prompt-based)\n   - §5.4: **Event Extraction (WikiEvents)** — cross-task generalization (D040)\n   - §5.5: Ablation + analysis (composability, latency, beam search, etc.)\n6. Related Work: 5 constraint paradigms (grammar, vocabulary, structural, type-checking, ontology) + event extraction methods\n7. Conclusion: Framework generality across IE tasks\n\n## Claim Calibration (per Reviewer assessment)\n\n**Safe to claim (sufficient evidence from Phase 2)**:\n- \"First systematic study of ontology constraint violations in LLM-based IE\"\n- \"Violation rate correlates with constraint tightness, not ontology size\" (D014: DR reduction ceiling 由 tightness × model RV baseline 共同决定)\n- \"Grammar+semantic constrained decoding eliminates 94% of DR violations at zero F1 cost\" ✅ Phase 2 confirmed\n- \"Two-layer architecture provides complementary coverage — grammar enables semantic\" ✅ Ablation confirmed\n- \"Prompt-level intervention scales poorly with ontology complexity\" ✅ SciERC ↓62% vs DocRED ↓32%\n\n**Claim with caution**:\n- \"Near-complete type-valid IE\" — S1 0.93%, S2 0.97% residual, not truly 0%. Title updated to \"Near-Complete\"\n- \"Principled framework applicable to arbitrary IE ontologies\" — RE validated on 2 datasets × 2 models; EE (WikiEvents) 10-doc preliminary shows ↓95.8% semantic violations, full results pending\n- \"F1 improvement\" — SciERC: not significant (p=0.58), frame as F1-neutral; DocRED: significant (+0.50pp, p<0.001), 可报告但不升级为 core claim，归因于 OOV elimination 而非约束解码本身的提升\n- \"CF reveals type system ambiguity\" — 可在 §5.3 作为 analysis finding 展开（Generic↔OtherScientificTerm 等模式有独立 insight 价值），但 §7 必须同时保留 CF 作为 limitation + future work。**两处都要有，缺一不可。** 不能暗示\"因为是 type ambiguity 所以 CF 可接受\"\n\n**Do NOT claim**:\n- \"General infrastructure for IE\" — only zero-shot extraction validated\n- \"State-of-the-art\" — F1 is control variable, not optimization target (see C8)\n- \"Synergistic effect\" — mechanism is enabling dependency, not mutual amplification (see Claim 3)\n- \"S2 solves CF\" or \"S2 mitigates Structure Snowballing\" — data shows S2 ≈ S1 on all metrics; position as architectural variant only\n- \"Pilot50 DR=0%\" — small-sample artifact, full S2 has DR=0.97%\n- \"Grammar-first invariant\" 作为独立 claim — 证据不足（仅 1 次崩溃触发，实现是 fallback 非形式化保证）。写入 §4 方法论设计原则（1-2 句），不升级为 claim\n- \"Robust dual-layer composition across schema complexities\" — 等 DocRED 完成。最终如 fallback ≤5/998，可写经验性陈述，不做泛化 claim\n\n## Risk Ranking (ordered by reject probability)\n\n1. **CF violation trade-off under-addressed** (MEDIUM-HIGH): S1 9.9%, S2 8.03% — both elevated. **S2 confirmed: does NOT solve CF.** This is the #1 attack surface. Mitigated by proactive disclosure + severity distinction + root cause analysis (C7). Must be reported as explicit limitation with future work direction (global entity-type consensus).\n2. ~~**Single model limitation**~~ (RESOLVED): Llama-3.1-8B SciERC ✅ (DR↓99.4%) + DocRED ✅ (DR↓90.2%). 2 模型 × 2 数据集全矩阵完成。\n3. **Novelty perception** (MEDIUM): \"PLDI'25 for code → OntoCoDec for IE\" attack line. Must argue IE constraint structure differs fundamentally.\n4. ~~**DocRED Phase 2 weak**~~ (RESOLVED → reframed as D014): Qwen DR↓44.7%, Llama DR↓90.2% — both substantial. Weaker Qwen reduction explained by RV baseline interaction (D014), not method failure.\n5. ~~**Phase 2 F1 drop**~~ (RESOLVED): F1 confirmed neutral (SciERC) or positive (DocRED, p<0.001). Bootstrap CI D012 confirms. No longer a risk.\n\n## Critical Path to EMNLP Submission (May 25)\n\n- **May 13-14**: Phase 0 + Phase 1 + Phase 2 SciERC ✅\n- **May 14**: Phase 2 DocRED 4-way ablation ✅ + Llama SciERC cross-model ✅ + Dream 完成 (3/6)\n- **May 14-15**: Llama DocRED ✅ + Checker 修正 ✅ + post-hoc ✅ + bootstrap CI ✅ + related work ✅\n- **May 15-17**: Prompt sensitivity ✅ + WikiEvents pipeline 开发 + continuation v2 突破\n- **May 17-18**: WikiEvents 3 模型 unconstrained baselines (进行中) + constrained 全量\n- **May 18-19**: WikiEvents 结果分析 + §5.4 Event Extraction 章节撰写\n- **May 19-20**: Intro/Abstract/Conclusion 升级（cross-task story）+ 内部稿 → submit_paper_to_review\n- **May 20-24**: Review 修改 + 最终提交\n\n**当前瓶颈**: WikiEvents 全量实验完成是关键路径。3 模型 unconstrained baselines 并行进行中（Qwen ~68/246, Mistral ~31/246, Llama 重启中），constrained 实验随后立即启动。\n\n## Status\n- Phase 0 SciERC: ✅ Complete (minimal + schema-informed)\n- Phase 0 DocRED: ✅ Complete (minimal 18.7% DR + schema-informed 12.8% DR)\n- Phase 1 Compiler: ✅ Complete (grammar + semantic layers integrated)\n- Phase 2 SciERC (5 configs): ✅ Complete (S1 DR↓94% F1-neutral, S2 降级为 ablation)\n- Phase 2 DocRED (4 configs): ✅ Complete (full_s1 DR↓45%, grammar ET/RV→0%)\n- Llama SciERC cross-model: ✅ Complete (DR↓99.4%, F1-neutral, 零代码修改)\n- Llama DocRED cross-model: ✅ Complete (full_s1 DR↓90.2%, unconstrained DR=26.07%)\n- Checker v2 (D011): ✅ Fixed (ET triple-counting → unique entity dedup)\n- Bootstrap CI (D012): ✅ Fixed + confirmed (entity filter bug resolved)\n- Post-hoc baseline (D013): ✅ Complete (multi-dimensional framing)\n- Related work: ✅ 42 bib entries, 4 additions merged\n- Dream 6/6 actions: ✅ All complete\n- CF violation analysis: ✅ Confirmed inherent limitation (S1 9.9% SciERC / 2.57% DocRED / 12.02% Llama DocRED)\n- D014 tightness revision: ✅ Complete (tightness × RV baseline dual-factor)\n- Llama bootstrap CI (D016): ✅ Fixed + verified (registry-aligned ≤0.05pp, all p-values in paper)\n- Paper compilation: ✅ 8 pages正文 + appendix\n- R5 text fixes (N1/N2/N3/W1-W6): ✅ All complete and verified\n- Prompt sensitivity analysis: ✅ Complete (3 prompts × 2 modes, DR reduction 94.0-94.6%, σ=0.3pp; appendix written)\n- Doc length breakdown: ✅ Complete (appendix written)\n- **WikiEvents Event Extraction (D040)**: 🔄 Continuation v2 突破 (10-doc: RoV 0%, semantic ↓95.8%); 3 模型 unconstrained baselines 进行中; constrained 全量待启动\n","numLines":311,"startLine":1,"totalLines":311}}}
